@vsavkin This seems to still be an issue if you first navigated to a route with { skipLocationChange: true }

```
this.router.navigate(['edit'], { relativeTo: this.route, skipLocationChange: true });
```

Then when you are about to navigate away and return `false`, the `/edit` creeps in the URL.

This is my routing:

```
path: 'view',
children: [
    {

        path: ':id',
        component: CustomerViewComponent,
        resolve: {
            customerViewData: CustomerResolve,
        },
        canDeactivate: [CanDeactivateGuard],
        children: [
            {
                path: 'edit',
            },
            {
                path: ''
            }
        ]
    }
]
```

Do you want to open a new bug for this?
